Watchdog service for MQTT topics to alert (via. email and ntfy) on inactivity thresholds, taking action (systemd service restart) if required,
and on the content of JSON messages (e.g. zigbee2mqtt device alarms, network device scans).

(0) read config file, and issue start up notification
(1) monitor configured topics for messages: track reception/timestamp
(2) if no message received on topic by
  (a) level 1 threshold, issue alert notification
  (b) level 2 threshold, issue alert notification and trigger systemd service restart
  (c) with topic.N.recover=true, issue a notification when messages resume
(3) watch configured alerts: an entity alerts while a JSON field has a given value
  (a) after it has held for alert.N.hold, issue alert notification
  (b) every alert.N.repeat while it holds, issue a reminder
  (c) when it clears, issue a recovery notification (alert.N.recover, default true)
(4) output periodic stats

Notifications go to each configured channel: email (email-*), and ntfy (ntfy-server, ntfy-topic, ntfy-token), with a priority
(min, low, default, high, urgent: topic.N.priority, alert.N.priority) and tags (emoji shortcodes: alert.N.tags).

Alerts (alert.N.*):

  topic      subscription, + and # wildcards allowed
  field      JSON field tested
  equals     value of the field that means alerting (as text: true, offline, ...)
  name       label in notifications (default: the field)
  array      optional: field holding an array of entries, each tracked on its own, named by
  key          its key field
  flags      optional: field of each entry holding flags; only entries flagged notifiable(hold/repeat) are watched,
               with those thresholds, and not those flagged ignore (as devices-known.conf)
  since      optional: field holding the local time the condition began (YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS), e.g. last_seen
  details    optional: comma-separated fields copied into notifications
  hold       how long it must hold before alerting (600, 45s, 30m, 3h, 1d; default 0)
  repeat     reminder interval while it holds (default 0: none)
  recover    notify when it clears (default true)

The entity is the part of the topic matched by wildcards (zigbee2mqtt/+ -> the device), or each array entry.
A field absent from a message leaves the entity alone, so zigbee2mqtt/+ with field smoke only watches devices
that report smoke. Instance configs (mqtt-watchdog-<instance>.cfg) hold credentials and are not committed.
